{
  "title": "Ziyarat of the Four Deputies of Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.)",
  "data": "At the tomb of any of the four deputies, begin by greeting the Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the Imams (a.s.):\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA A'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIB\nPeace be upon the Commander of the Faithful, Ali son of Abi Talib.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى خَدِيْجَةَ الْكُبْرٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA KHADEEJATAL KUBRAA\nPeace be upon Khadijah al-Kubra.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'\nPeace be upon Fatimah al-Zahra.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL HASANIBNI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon al-Hasan son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحُسَيْنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL HUSAYNIBNI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon al-Husayn son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon Ali son of al-Husayn.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon Muhammad son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA JA'FARIBNI MUHAMMAD\nPeace be upon Ja'far son of Muhammad.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MOOSABNI JA'FAR\nPeace be upon Musa son of Ja'far.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA A'LIYYIBNI MOOSAA\nPeace be upon Ali son of Musa.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon Muhammad son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA A'LIYYIBNI MUHAMMAD\nPeace be upon Ali son of Muhammad.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL HASANIBNI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon al-Hasan son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ الْحَسَنِ الْمَهْدِيِّ صَاحِبِ الزَّمَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIBNIL HASANIL MAHDIYYI SAAHIBIZ ZAMAAN\nPeace be upon Muhammad son of al-Hasan al-Mahdi, the Master of the Age.\nThen greet the deputy, naming him and his father in place of fulan ibn fulan: Uthman ibn Sa'id, Muhammad ibn Uthman, Husayn ibn Ruh or Ali ibn Muhammad:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA FULAANABNA FULAAN\nPeace be upon you, O (name) son of (name).\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ بَابُ الْمَوْلٰى\nASH-HADU ANNAKA BAABUL MAWLAA\nI bear witness that you are verily the door to the Chief;\nاَدَّيْتَ عَنْهُ وَاَدَّيْتَ اِلَيْهِ\nADDAYTA A'NHU WA ADDAYTA ILAYH\nyou conveyed on behalf of him and conveyed to him;\nمَا خَالَفْتَهٗ وَلَا خَالَفْتَ عَلَيْهِ\nMAA KHAALAFTAHOO WA LAA KHAALAFTA A'LAYH\nyou neither contradicted him nor disagreed with him.\nقُمْتَ خَآصًّا وَانْصَرَفْتَ سَابِقًا\nQUMTA KHAASSAN WANSARAFTA SAABIQAA\nYou represented him individually and passed away excelling all others.\nجِئْتُكَ عَارِفًا بِالْحَقِّ الَّذِيۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِ\nJI'TUKA A'ARIFAN BIL HAQQIL LADHEE ANTA A'LAYH\nI have come to you, recognizing the truth you are following\nوَاَنَّكَ مَا خُنْتَ فِي التَّاْدِيَةِ وَالسِّفَارَةِ\nWA ANNAKA MAA KHUNTA FIT TA'DIYATI WAS SIFAARAH\nand understanding that you have never cheated in conveyance and in representation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ بَابٍ مَا اَوْسَعَكَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN BAABIN MAA AWSA'AK\nPeace be upon you; you are a door opened extremely wide,\nوَمِنْ سَفِيْرٍ مَاۤ اٰمَنَكَ وَمِنْ ثِقَةٍ مَاۤ اَمْكَنَكَ\nWA MIN SAFEERIN MAA AAMANAKA WA MIN THIQATIN MAA AMKANAK\nan emissary trusted immeasurably, and a very versed trustworthy.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اخْتَصَّكَ بِنُوْرِهٖ حَتّٰى عَايَنْتَ الشَّخْصَ\nASH-HADU ANNALLAAHAKH TASSAKA BINOORIHEE HATTAA A'AYANTASH SHAKHS\nI bear witness that Allah has given you His light so exclusively that you could see (the Imam) in person;\nفَاَدَّيْتَ عَنْهُ وَاَدَّيْتَ اِلَيْهِ.\nFA-ADDAYTA A'NHU WA ADDAYTA ILAYH\nyou therefore conveyed on behalf of him and conveyed to him.\nThen repeat the greetings from the Messenger of Allah to the Imam of the Age (a.t.f.s.), and say:\nجِئْتُكَ مُخْلِصًا بِتَوْحِيْدِ اللّٰهِ وَمُوَالَاةِ اَوْلِيَاۤئِهٖ\nJI'TUKA MUKHLISAN BITAWHEEDILLAAHI WA MUWAALAATI AWLIYAA'IH\nI have come to you professing Allah’s being the One and Only Lord, declaring loyalty to His loyalists,\nوَالْبَرَاۤءَةِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِهٖ وَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَالَفُوْكَ\nWAL BARAA'ATI MIN A'DAA'IHEE WA MINAL LADHEENA KHAALAFOOK\nand declaring repudiation from His enemies and those who dissented you,\nيَا حُجَّةَ الْمَوْلٰى\nYAA HUJJATAL MAWLAA\nO Argument of the Chief.\nوَبِكَ اِلَيْهِمْ تَوَجُّهِيْ\nWA BIKA ILAYHIM TAWAJJUHEE\nThrough you do I turn my face to them\nوَبِهِمْ اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَسُّلِيْ.\nWA BIHIM ILALLAAHI TAWASSULEE\nand through them do I seek means to Allah.\nThen pray and ask Allah for whatever you wish; it will be granted, Allah willing.",
  "merits": "Shaykh al-Tusi, in Tahdhib al-Ahkam, and Sayyid Ibn Tawus, in Misbah al-Za’ir, report this form of ziyarat of the tombs of the Four Deputies from Abu’l-Qasim Husayn ibn Rawh. It is recited at the tomb of each of them, naming him.\n\nThe Four Emissaries of Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) are Abu-’Amr ‘Uthman ibn Sa’id al-Asadi, Abu-Ja’far Muhammad ibn ‘Uthman, Shaykh Abu’l-Qasim Husayn ibn Rawh al-Nawbakhti, and the sublime Shaykh Abu’l-Hasan ‘Ali ibn Muhammad al-Samari, may Allah be pleased with them all.\n\nOne of the duties of the visitors of the holy shrines in Iraq is to come to Baghdad, during their stay at al-Kazimiyyah city, for visiting the Four Emissaries who represented the Awaited Argument of Allah and the Imam of the Age, peace of Allah be upon him. Visiting the tombs of these personalities does not require much effort, because they are all situated in near places in Baghdad; therefore, they are not far away for the visitors. However, even if these graves were scattering in remote places, they would be worthy of being visited by covering long distances and suffering the troubles of travel, because great reward and abundant prize are gained from visiting these graves.\n\nThe Four Emissaries excelled all the companions and elite friends of the Holy Imams (a.s.) in rank and excellence. They thus won the Imam’s representation, emissary, and mediation between him and the subjects for seventy years. They also showed many extraordinary manners and innumerable miracles. Moreover, some scholars are reported to have imputed Divinely-granted infallibility (i.e. ‘ismah) to these personalities.\n\nIt goes without saying that these personalities are still mediators between the Imam (a.s.) and the subjects after their death; it is therefore necessary to make them the means and way to convey to the Imam, in a written form, the needs and ordeals from which his subjects suffer.\n\nIn conclusion, no pen can contain the great merits and supreme statuses of these personalities."
}
